<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  T08 Guarded Flow

  A REAL FUNCTION BLOCK: numbered steps, a guard that compares two values of
  the SAME quantity, a goto, and a fall-through end. This is what the State
  Machine view reads — one state per sequence, one transition per goto.

  A UNIT TEST DESIGN. Bundled with the app and read-only: suite [25]
  asserts what this file is supposed to prove, so editing it here
  changes what the harness tests.
-->
<gorp name="T08 Guarded Flow">
  <!-- nos-uml-state {"mode":"ai-design","title":"T08 Guarded Flow","layout":{"ut.flow.In":{"x":60,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.flow.Gate":{"x":420,"y":60,"w":300,"h":160},"ut.flow.Out":{"x":800,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140}}} -->

  <comment view="class">A real function block. Gate's function has three numbered steps: step 0 compares level against limit — both in metres, so the guard is legal — and jumps to step 2 when it passes; step 1 refuses; step 2 accepts.

This is what the State Machine view reads: one state per sequence, one transition per goto. Select Gate and switch to it.</comment>
  <expect>Check finds nothing.

The State Machine view shows three states and the goto as a guarded transition; the Sequence view shows In into Gate and Gate out to Out.

Compare two different quantities inside the guard and Check must refuse it the way N01 is refused.</expect>
  <model namespace="ut.flow.In">
    <variables>
      <variable name="level" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\metre" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="limit" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\metre" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
    </variables>
  </model>

  <algorithm namespace="ut.flow.Gate">
    <input  model="ut.flow.In" />
    <output model="ut.flow.Out" />
    <operations>
      <operation name="gate" returns="bool" />
    </operations>
    <function>
      <expressions>
        <expression sequence="0" name="over the limit?">
          <If input="ut.flow.In">
            <parameters>
              <parameter position="0">
                <Less input="ut.flow.In" output="ut.flow.Out.passed">
                  <parameters>
                    <parameter position="0"><pathvariable type="double" namespace="ut.flow.In.level"/></parameter>
                    <parameter position="1"><pathvariable type="double" namespace="ut.flow.In.limit"/></parameter>
                  </parameters>
                </Less>
              </parameter>
              <parameter position="1"><goto sequence="2"/></parameter>
            </parameters>
          </If>
        </expression>
        <expression sequence="1" name="refuse" />
        <expression sequence="2" name="accept" />
      </expressions>
    </function>
  </algorithm>

  <model namespace="ut.flow.Out">
    <variables>
      <variable name="passed" type="bool" />
    </variables>
  </model>
</gorp>
